@*
    Shown when an unauthenticated user reaches a protected route. Deliberately not an instant
    auto-redirect: an invisible bounce straight to the Entra ID challenge endpoint leaves nobody
    a way to reach Emergency Access if SSO itself is what's broken. This gives every signed-out
    visitor a real landing page with both options.
*@

<div class="login-backdrop">
    <div class="breakglass-login accent-brand">
        <div class="notice-logo">
            <img src="img/emirates-glass-logo.png" alt="Emirates Glass" class="panel-logo" />
            <span class="notice-brand">Manpower Allocation</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Sign in required</h1>
        <p class="hint">Sign in with your organisation account to continue.</p>

        <FluentAnchor Href="MicrosoftIdentity/Account/SignIn" Appearance="Appearance.Accent" Style="width:100%; justify-content:center">
            Sign in with your organisation account
        </FluentAnchor>

        <p class="login-foot">
            Trouble signing in? <a href="break-glass">Emergency access</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
